{
  "id": "brief-psychodynamic-psychotherapy",
  "term": "brief psychodynamic psychotherapy",
  "definition": "Brief psychodynamic psychotherapy is a time-limited form of psychodynamic therapy that is organized around one or more clear treatment focuses rather than broad, long-term aims. It requires the therapist to take an active role, establish the focus early, work on it consistently in the present therapeutic relationship, and set goals that are realistic within a limited time.",
